    "result": "I implemented `RateLimiter` in `solution.py` and left the signatures and class name unchanged. Each client gets a deque of `(time, cost)` entries, oldest first. Every method first validates its arguments and then checks `now` against the largest time seen so far by the limiter, which raises `ValueError` if time goes backwards. Expired entries (where `now - t >= window_seconds`) are dropped before the budget is measured, so a request exactly `window_seconds` old no longer counts. `allow` appends only when it accepts, while `remaining` and `retry_after` record nothing. `retry_after` walks the live entries oldest first to find the one whose expiry frees enough units for the cost, and returns the gap from `now` to that expiry. I also rejected NaN times and made the constructor and cost checks refuse `bool`, as the spec requires. Nothing was run or tested, since shell access was not available and the task said not to write tests.",
